description:
Returns the mix and pressure a cylinder ends with after gases are added in order: each addition's pressure and mix before and after, the cooling step, and the final O₂ %, He % and pressure. Use this when a diver or blender asks what a fill produced ("50 bar of air, 40 bar of oxygen, then air to 200"), or to check a plan_blend plan: send its mix_result_current as current and its mix_result_additions as additions. Not for planning toward a target (plan_blend) or joining two cylinders with a whip (decant).

Pressures are gauge (bar or psi, per units); mixes are O₂ % and He %. environment sets altitude and the ambient and fill temperatures (defaults sea level, 20 °C, fill equal to ambient); a hot fill settles lower. Real-gas mixing. Analyse the cylinder once it has cooled: the analysed mix, not this one, goes into plan_dive. No engine call.

Example: {"current":{"oxygen_pct":21,"pressure":50},"additions":[{"oxygen_pct":100,"pressure_added":35},{"oxygen_pct":21,"pressure_added":115}]}
